00:13:43.709 --> 00:13:46.880
hundred thousand Americans die.

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:49.449
That's that's a system that works really well.

00:13:49.449 --> 00:13:54.649
I lived in Germany in the nineteen eighties
when their health care system was still largely

00:13:54.649 --> 00:13:58.160
ninety nine percent, really just a single
payer system.

00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:04.790
What happened and the reason why you're seeing
all this so-called diversity, David, is that

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:08.689
in the eighties there was this major project
launched.

00:14:08.689 --> 00:14:14.139
It really was launched in nineteen seventy
eight by Margaret Thatcher in the UK and but

00:14:14.139 --> 00:14:19.699
by the 80s it had become a whole new governing
paradigm that is sometimes referred to as

00:14:19.699 --> 00:14:21.509
neo liberalism.

00:14:21.509 --> 00:14:25.009
And its core tenet is that government can't
do anything right.

00:14:25.009 --> 00:14:29.449
As Reagan said in nineteen eighty eight January
20th of eighty one when he was inaugurated,

00:14:29.449 --> 00:14:30.480
government is not the problem.

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:34.160
Government is the cause of the problems, not
the solution to the problem.

00:14:34.160 --> 00:14:42.069
And so as country after country adopted what
are called neo liberal reforms, and as the

00:14:42.069 --> 00:14:49.970
EU began to incorporate neo liberal policies
into their charter, they required countries,

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:59.069
for example, not exceed three percent of debt
in GDP, debt of three percent of debt relative

00:14:59.069 --> 00:15:00.069
to GDP.

00:15:00.069 --> 00:15:05.089
In any given year, et cetera, you know, the
stuff that just brought Greece to its knees

00:15:05.089 --> 00:15:11.399
during the crash in 2009, as that happened,
more and more countries started.

00:15:11.399 --> 00:15:15.759
You know, one of the biggest pieces of neoliberalism,
of course, is privatizing government functions

00:15:15.759 --> 00:15:18.060
on the assumption government can't do anything
right.

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:22.120
It's why more than half of our power and water
in the cities is not provided by for profit

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:27.662
companies, which is also why, you know, California
burned and maybe three people died in the

00:15:27.662 --> 00:15:30.740
Paradise Fire, which PG&amp;E was convicted of.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:36.750
And why the high tension lines down south
going to New Orleans never got buried because

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:38.129
they had to pay their stockholders.

00:15:38.129 --> 00:15:44.910
But anyhow, that that neoliberal infection
was caught by a number of European countries,

00:15:44.910 --> 00:15:52.350
most notably France and Germany and the U.K.,
I think to a large part succeeded in pushing

00:15:52.350 --> 00:15:56.510
it away, which is kind of ironic because so
much of this started with Maggie Thatcher.

00:15:56.510 --> 00:15:57.779
But that's what you're looking at.

00:15:57.779 --> 00:16:04.149
You're looking at experiments in bringing
more and more so-called free market stuff

00:16:04.149 --> 00:16:05.800
into health care.

00:16:05.800 --> 00:16:08.930
And many of them are just not working well
at all.

00:16:08.930 --> 00:16:13.910
Speaker 1: Yes, that is an understatement,
to say the least.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:18.410
We've been talking about Tom Hartmans latest
book, The Hidden History of American Health

00:16:18.410 --> 00:16:22.680
